README.md:30:- **Open voices**: a local OpenAI-compatible server is a declared provider (`keyless: true`, `allow_insecure_endpoint: "127.0.0.1"`; one endpoint rule in cheval, the bash validator and `model-health-probe.sh --provider <name>`), the chat path sends `response_format` json_schema and strips thinking traces honestly, `advisory_voices` run beside the dissent's counted voices and can never change a verdict, and `hounfour.locality: local_voices` refuses every hosted hop by name across the dissent, Flatline, Bridgebuilder and the probe. Bridgebuilder reads providers only from trusted configuration, prints `completed/planned` voices and exits 3 on a degraded consensus.
.claude/loa/reference/multi-model-reference.md:102:cycle-129 (FR-8) — **local posture**: under `hounfour.locality: local_voices` the dissent, Flatline, Bridgebuilder and health-probe hops are planned only on providers whose model entry says `dispatch_group: local`, each hosted hop refused by name at plan time; the Claude Code session model is exempt and remains the platform, so a local posture keeps model calls local but the session itself still runs against Anthropic. Fewer voices means a DEGRADED verdict quality where the planned voice count is not met — the posture says so in the config comment and in the run output rather than inventing a voice. One fail-closed classifier (`.claude/scripts/lib/hop-locality.py`) serves the shell scripts: an unresolved hop, an unreadable config or a local entry whose fallback chain reaches a hosted entry counts as hosted; an invalid value refuses the run.
.claude/loa/reference/multi-model-reference.md:104:cycle-129 (FR-7) — **open-weight and local voices**: a local OpenAI-compatible server is declared as a provider (`type: openai_compat`, `keyless: true`, `allow_insecure_endpoint: "<host>"` where the host is a loopback or RFC1918 IP literal or `localhost`; Example 4 in `.loa.config.yaml.example`). The endpoint rule lives once in `.claude/scripts/lib/endpoint-validator.py` and is used by the cheval loader (`loa_cheval/config/endpoint_policy.py`), the bash wrapper and `model-health-probe.sh --provider <name>`, which probes a configured provider's `/models` with no credential when keyless; at request time a local hop runs with no proxy, no redirects and the declared path prefix. cheval refuses an `http`, loopback or private endpoint without the opt-in at load, for every provider. On the chat-completions path a `structured_json` entry sends `response_format` json_schema and `schema_enforced` is derived from the body sent (one retry without the schema on a server 400 that names it); `reasoning_content`, `reasoning` deltas and a leading `<think>` block go to `thinking` (`thinking_stripped`); an over-window prompt is refused by name. **Advisory voices**: `flatline_protocol.code_review.advisory_voices` and `security_audit.advisory_voices` run beside the counted voices under `advisory_timeout_seconds`; their findings appear only under `advisory_voices[].findings` with `duplicate_of` links and never touch the verdict, the counts or the cost totals — promotion to a counted role needs `hounfour.advisory_promotion`. The budget gate prices each planned voice from the catalog (`loa_cheval.metering.pricing --alias … --json`), whose entries now carry `open_weight`, `price_source` and `price_date`. **Bridgebuilder** reads `hounfour.providers`, `hounfour.locality` and `bridgebuilder.exit_on_degraded` from trusted configuration only (locally the working tree; on a pull request the `BRIDGEBUILDER_TRUSTED_CONFIG` repository variable, else the base branch's config, never the head), prints `completed/planned` voices and exits 3 on a DEGRADED consensus (`0` restores the old exit; `entry.sh`'s dependency preflight exits 4).
